{"created": "2026-06-16T14:03:57.076585+00:00", "modified": "2026-06-16T14:03:57.356942+00:00", "id": 20719043, "conceptrecid": "20719042", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20719043", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.20719042", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20719043", "metadata": {"title": "An explicit exponential-period representation of the V_quad connection coefficient", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.20719043", "publication_date": "2026-06-16", "description": "<p>We prove that the connection coefficient C of the V_quad polynomial continued fraction&mdash;the rank-one standalone closure on the Sakai surface D\u2085\u207d&sup1;\u207e (Painlev&eacute; V)&mdash;admits an explicit exponential-period representation C=(|&Gamma;(&beta;)|/2&pi;)&int;_&gamma; e^&xi; B\u0302(&xi;) d&xi;=|&Gamma;(&beta;)| K, where B\u0302 is the Borel transform of the V_quad asymptotic series, holonomic of order 4 (the Borel&ndash;Laplace dual of the order-2 operator annihilating the series) with coefficients in the real quadratic field \u211a(&radic;3); &gamma; is an explicit Hankel rapid-decay cycle on (&minus;&infin;,&minus;2/&radic;3]; and &beta;=&minus;1/(3&radic;3). The identity is verified by three structurally independent methods&mdash;differential-equation/operator duality, Borel&ndash;Laplace contour deformation, and Stokes-data&mdash;agreeing to 46 digits. The order-2 operator annihilating the asymptotic series has differential Galois group SL\u2082(\u2102) by Kovacic's algorithm. As a by-product, holonomicity of the Borel transform forces a finite resurgent structure. Finally, conditional on the Fres&aacute;n&ndash;Jossen period conjecture for exponential motives and on a stated motivic-comparison hypothesis, C is transcendental over \u211a\u0304. This record accompanies the VQUAD-PERIODREP reproducibility bundle (verification scripts, certificates, and a byte-reproducible build), which reproduces every numerical claim above, including the 46-digit agreement. The work was produced under the SIARC governance methodology; per-stage provenance and AEAL-level claim ledgers are linked from the bundle's SIARC_PROVENANCE.md. The identity continues the V_quad companion paper (concept DOI 10.5281/zenodo.20455089) within the Sakai Stratification of PCF Transcendence program.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Papanokechi", "affiliation": "Independent Researcher", "orcid": "0009-0000-6192-8273"}], "keywords": ["polynomial continued fractions", "exponential periods", "Painlev\u00e9 V", "Fres\u00e1n-Jossen exponential motives", "Borel-Laplace duality", "conditional transcendence", "Sakai stratification", "motivic Galois group"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.20455089", "relation": "continues", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.20694840", "relation": "continues", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.19885549", "relation": "isPartOf", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.20569723", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.20566465", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.20624813", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/s002200100446", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1016/S0747-7171(86)80010-4", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1007/s00220-024-05187-0", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1016/j.geomphys.2017.10.009", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.1063/5.0002260", "relation": "references", "resource_type": "publication-article", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "1.0", "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/papanokechi/project-fingerprint", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "lean", "title": {"en": "Lean"}}, {"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}], "code:developmentStatus": {"id": "active", "title": {"en": "Active"}}}, "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": false, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "20719042"}}]}}, "title": "An explicit exponential-period representation of the V_quad connection coefficient", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20719043", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20719043", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20719043?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20719043", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20719043", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.20719043", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20719043/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20719042", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/20719042", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20719042", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.20719042", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20719043/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20719043/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20719043/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/20719043/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20719043:vquad-periodrep-paper.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20719043:vquad-periodrep-paper.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:20719043:vquad-periodrep-paper.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default